The U.S. state of [[South Dakota]] first required its residents to register their [[motor vehicle]]s in 1905. Registrants provided their own [[Vehicle registration plate|license plate]]s for display until 1913, when the state began to issue plates.<ref>{{cite web |title=Old South Dakota License Plates |url=http://leatherlicenseplates.com/old-south-dakota-license-plates-vintage-south-dakota-license-plates/ |publisher=LeatherLicensePlates.com |date=<!-- Deny Citation Bot--> |access-date=July 21, 2017}}</ref>

{{As of|2024}}, plates are issued by the South Dakota Department of Revenue through its Motor Vehicle Division. Front and rear plates are required for most classes of vehicles, while only rear plates are required for motorcycles and trailers.

